{Game score not available. Mortimer, playing a queen's opening against Curnock,
sacrificed material, as usual, to break through. Afterwards he simplified
matters by losing his queen, and resigned. London Daily News, 27 JUL 1904, p.
11  Mortimer gave up a piece for three passed Pawns, and would have certainly
won the game but for an oversight. London Evening Standard, 27 JUL 1904, p. 7 
Mortimer declined the Queen's Gambit offered by Curnock, and after obtaining a
good position lost to a miscaculation. London Morning Post, 27 JUL 1904, p. 6} 
1-0

