{Game score not available. Philidor Defence. Mason won a pawn, and brought it
down to a Rook and Pawn ending, and won after a hard fight. Mueller had a
slight advantage in the early part, and could have simply concenrated his
forces on Black's weak Queen's Pawn, taking precautions that he should not
advance it. London Evening Standard, 4 AUG 1904, p. 9}  0-1

