{Game score not available. Lee defended with the Caro-Kann against Loman, who
obtained a good position, but lost a pawn by pressing too rapidly. Lee
afterwards increased the advantage, and a long end game ensued, in which he
had rook and four pawns to rook and three, Loman resigning on the 59th move.
London Daily News, 5 AUG 1904, p. 11}  0-1

