{Game score not available. Van Vliet played the King's Bishop Opening against
Curnock, who got a bad position in the middle game. He attempted some
counterattack, the chief result of which was to get a rook in an akward place,
requiring loss of time to extricate it. Van Vliet won on the 44th move. London
Daily News, 5 AUG 1904, p. 11}  1-0

