{Game score not available Three Knights Game. Mason had a position which
looked, and in fact was, utterly hopeless. He went on, however, nothing
daunted, and Blackburne, playing timidly, let him off with a draw, by allowing
him to exchange the attacking forces. London Evening Standard, 6 AUG 1904, p. 3
}  1/2-1/2

