{The first game to be concluded was between Mortimer and Van Vliet. The latter
player has had a good deal of luck in this tournament, and once more managed
to win what shoud have been a lost game, owing to weak play at the decisive
moment by Mortimer. source: Yorkshire Telegraph and Star, 9 AUG 1904, p. 4} 1.
